{
  "_meta": {
    "schema_version": 1,
    "spec": "The catalog split, a physical boundary",
    "merchant": "Aether Audio",
    "currency": "INR",
    "amount_unit": "whole rupees, integer, no paise anywhere in the system",
    "sku_count": 14,
    "notes": [
      "Two arrays, not one nested object: `products` is safe to serialize to any buyer, `product_private` never leaves the server. Joined on `sku`. The split is structural so a loader bug cannot leak private economics by forgetting to strip a nested key.",
      "`products` rows carry exactly the seven public fields and nothing else. Any new field is a decision about what buyers may see.",
      "`offerable` lives in product_private: it is a merchant policy flag, and the oversell saga flips it to false during self-heal. A non-offerable SKU is omitted from catalog responses rather than shown as unavailable.",
      "AT-TIP-FOAM ships with stock_qty 0 on purpose — it is the fixture for the out-of-stock rejection test, and it is an attach candidate, so the rejection lands on an upsell while the base item proceeds.",
      "AT-STUDIO-PRO ships with stock_qty 3 to make stock-hold contention and the oversell race reachable without editing rows by hand.",
      "AT-PRO-BLK (4999) + AT-CASE-01 (599) = 5598, the exact amount in the compensation walkthrough. 3 x 4999 = 14997, the Tier-2 routing case."
    ]
  },

